course: dictionary
lesson: 3731
title: One word, two jobs: flock
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A flock is a group of birds or sheep that stay together. A shepherd looks after his flock on the hills. Flock can also be a verb: «people flocked to the beach» means people came together in large numbers.
explain: The same spelling can do two jobs. In «a flock of sheep», flock names a group, so it is a noun. In «people flocked to the beach», flock shows what people did, so it is a verb. Ask yourself: is this word naming something, or describing an action?
explain: Phrases carry meaning too. «Birds of a feather flock together» is an idiom. It does not mean real birds; it means people who are alike like to spend time together. When a sentence sounds odd word for word, look for the meaning behind it.
fact: A flock is a group of birds or sheep together.
fact: A flock can also be a big crowd of people.
fact: To flock means to come together or go somewhere in large numbers.
fact: The verb forms are flock, flocks, flocked and flocking.
fact: «Birds of a feather flock together» means similar people stay together.
exercise: «A shepherd looks after his flock on the hills.» What is a flock here? | A tall wooden stick | A kind of whistle | *A group of sheep | A sunny field
exercise: «People flocked to the beach when the sun came out.» What does flocked mean? | Were sad and tired | *Came together in large numbers | Fell asleep on the sand | Stayed at home alone
exercise: «Wild parrots copy the calls of their flock.» What does flock mean? | *A group of birds living together | A loud whistle | A type of sunny weather | A big stone
test: «Her kind once flew in flocks of billions that darkened the sky.» What does flocks mean here? | Pigeons in a glass case | Dark clouds in the morning | *Large groups of birds flying together | Very small nests
test: Choose the right word: Yesterday, shoppers ___ to the sale. | flock | flocks | *flocked
exam: Which sentence uses flock as a verb? | «The shepherd counted his sheep.» | *«Fans flocked to the stadium before the match.» | «A flock of starlings filled the sky.» | «The flock grazed quietly on the hill.»
